.TH SXFER 1 "2026-10-05" "sxfer 2.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sxfer \- high-speed, one-way serial file tree transfer using concatenated SC-LDPC, RaptorQ fountain coding, and LZMA2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sxfer send
.RI [ options ]
.IR PATH ...
.br
.B sxfer recv
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sxfer daemon
.RI [ --config " " CONF ]
.br
.B sxfer systemd install
.br
.B sxfer tray
.RI [ --config " " CONF ]
.br
.B sxfer crc
.IR FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sxfer
copies complete directory hierarchies and file trees across a one-way (simplex / TX-only) serial link
(such as USB-to-UART, RS-485, optical isolators, or unidirectional data diodes).
There is no reverse channel, no ACKs/NACKs, and no backpressure handshake.
.PP
To ensure maximum throughput, zero transmission gaps, and robust erasure recovery under extreme channel noise,
.B sxfer
integrates:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB100% Pure Rust & Static Musl Architecture\fR: Zero C runtime dependencies; compiled as a single standalone static binary.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInner Rate 2/3 SC-QC-LDPC FEC\fR: Quasi-Cyclic Spatially-Coupled Low-Density Parity-Check codes with Belief Propagation and anti-oscillation momentum, correcting 5\(en10% Bit Error Rate (BER).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOuter Rateless Fountain Coding (RaptorQ over GF(256))\fR: Systematic fountain encoding with multi-block interleaving, recovering from packet drop rates exceeding 80%.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHigh-Ratio Fast LZMA2 Level 9 Compression\fR: Integrated pure-Rust dictionary compression enforced on all transmitted streams.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWatch Directory Spooling (\-w DIR)\fR: Continuous filesystem monitoring with automatic debouncing, queuing, transmission, and post-transfer cleanup.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUnified Baseband Framing & Line Whitening\fR: Consistent Overhead Byte Stuffing (COBS) with 0x00 frame boundaries and Galois LFSR 16-bit scrambler to prevent bit stuffing loss and clock drift.
.PP
.B sxfer send
walks each
.IR PATH ,
compresses files using LZMA2 Level 9, encodes fountain symbols and SC-LDPC frames, and streams them through the pipeline.
Paths are transmitted relative to the working directory.
.PP
.B sxfer recv
runs on the receiving machine and should be started before the sender.
It reconstructs files, verifies 32-bit CRC checksums, and applies directory hierarchies, permissions, timestamps, and symlinks.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS send
.TP
.BI \-d " DEV"
Serial device or output file/FIFO (default
.BR /dev/ttyUSB0 ).
.TP
.BI \-b " BAUD"
Baud rate from 1200 up to 4000000+ (default
.BR 115200 ).
.TP
.BI \-w " DIR"
Watch directory mode: automatically creates \fIDIR\fR if not existed, continuously monitors it for incoming files or directory trees, transmits them over the serial line with RaptorQ protection, and deletes them upon successful transfer.
.TP
.BI \-c " BYTES"
Symbol chunk size in bytes (16 to 65536). If omitted or 0, chunk size is chosen adaptively based on baud rate.
.TP
.BI \-f " PCT"
Extra RaptorQ fountain repair symbols to generate as a percentage of source symbols (default
.BR 35 ).
.TP
.BI \-r " ROUNDS"
Number of transmission rounds (default
.BR 1 ).
.TP
.B \-h
Display help summary.
.SS recv
.TP
.BI \-d " DEV"
Serial device or input FIFO (default
.BR /dev/ttyUSB0 ).
.TP
.BI \-b " BAUD"
Baud rate (default
.BR 115200 ).
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Destination directory for received files (default
.BR ./recv ).
.TP
.BI \-q " SEC"
Quit after
.I SEC
seconds of line silence (default: 0 = loop indefinitely).
.TP
.B \-p
Restore original file owner and group (requires root).
.TP
.B \-h
Display help summary.
.SS daemon
.TP
.B sxfer daemon \fR[\fB\-\-config \fICONF\fR]
Run sxfer as a background service daemon according to
.IR /etc/sxfer.conf
(or the configuration file specified by \fICONF\fR).
.SS systemd
.TP
.B sxfer systemd install
Generate default configuration at \fI/etc/sxfer.conf\fR, install systemd service unit at \fI/etc/systemd/system/sxfer.service\fR, and reload systemd.
.SS tray
.TP
.B sxfer tray \fR[\fB\-\-config \fICONF\fR]
Run sxfer in Windows System Tray notification area background service mode.
.SS crc
.TP
.B sxfer crc \fIFILE\fR
Compute and print the standard IEEE 802.3 CRC-32 checksum of
.IR FILE .
.SH RECOVERY & VERIFICATION
.TP
.B RaptorQ Rateless Fountain Coding
Files are divided into source blocks with K <= 128 symbols.
The receiver accumulates incoming symbols and performs Gaussian elimination over GF(256) as soon as K independent symbols are received.
Packet drops during transmission do not require retransmission; any subsequent repair symbol replaces any lost source symbol.
.TP
.B Frame Checking
Each transmitted frame contains a dedicated 32-bit CRC covering the packet contents. Corrupted frames caused by electrical noise are dropped immediately before reaching the decoder.
.TP
.B File Integrity
The end-to-end CRC-32 of every source file is verified upon reassembly and decompression prior to final atomic renaming.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a directory tree over a 2.0 Mbaud RS-485 line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxfer send -d /dev/ttyUSB0 -b 2000000 src/ assets/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Receive the files into
.IR /opt/data :
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxfer recv -d /dev/ttyUSB0 -b 2000000 -o /opt/data -q 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Test transfers over an IPC named pipe:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkfifo /tmp/wire
sxfer recv -d /tmp/wire -o /tmp/dst -q 2 &
sxfer send -d /tmp/wire -f 30 file1.bin dir2/
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR termios (3),
.BR stty (1)